{#
  The one page banner — the dark hero strip with a heading, an optional blurb
  and an optional bleed image on the right.

  It existed nine times: page.njk, meet-the-team.njk, sitemap.njk, 404.njk,
  post-archive.njk, search.njk, post.njk, personnel.njk and location.njk. The
  copies had drifted in three ways that only a side-by-side showed:

    * two names for the same wrapper — `page-banner-content-container` in five
      of them and `page-banner-container` in four. NEITHER has a CSS rule
      (style.css styles .page-banner, .page-banner-content, .page-banner-title
      and .page-banner-figure; `container` does the layout), so the split was
      pure copy-paste drift with no effect either way. The majority spelling is
      kept here.
    * the <figure> was guarded in four and unguarded in two, so a record with no
      banner_image rendered <img src="">.
    * location.njk carried an entirely empty content block.

  Takes one options object so callers read as named arguments:

    {{ pageBanner({ title: "Careers", image: "/assets/img/pages/careers.jpg" }) }}

    title          text for the <h1>
    titleHtml      markup appended inside the <h1> (search.njk's live query span)
    parentHref     renders a "back to <parentLabel>" link INSTEAD of an <h1>.
    parentLabel    Post and personnel pages put their own <h1> in the body, so
                   this must not be a heading — as an <h2> it sat above the
                   page's own <h1> on 304 pages.
    description    plain text, wrapped in <p>
    descriptionHtml  pre-rendered markup, used as-is
    image          banner image; omitted entirely when absent
    thumb          also tag that image as the page's Pagefind thumbnail
    pagefindIgnore keep the whole banner out of the search index
#}
{% macro pageBanner(o) %}
<section class="page-banner"{% if o.pagefindIgnore %} data-pagefind-ignore{% endif %}>
	<div class="page-banner-content">
		<div class="page-banner-content-container container">
			{%- if o.parentHref %}
			<p class="page-banner-title"><a class="page-banner-title-link" href="{{ o.parentHref }}">{{ o.parentLabel }}</a></p>
			{%- elif o.title or o.titleHtml %}
			<h1 class="page-banner-title">{{ o.title }}{{ o.titleHtml | safe }}</h1>
			{%- endif %}
			{%- if o.descriptionHtml %}
			<div class="content">{{ o.descriptionHtml | safe }}</div>
			{%- elif o.description %}
			<div class="content"><p>{{ o.description }}</p></div>
			{%- endif %}
		</div>
	</div>
	{%- if o.image %}
	<figure class="page-banner-figure"><img src="{{ o.image }}" alt="" class="page-banner-image"{% if o.thumb %} data-pagefind-meta="image[src]"{% endif %}></figure>
	{%- endif %}
</section>
{% endmacro %}
